enum TaskPaymentClaimStatus {
  PENDING
  PURCHASED
  REFUNDED
}

/// VERIFIED is terminal for the automated flow (PR1-SPEC §4): the node signs
/// the X-PAYMENT header locally and Soko cannot observe settlement, so nothing
/// may auto-progress a VERIFIED record until the phased-settlement reconciler
/// (ticket 011 Q3) ships. REFUNDED is reached from PENDING (stale-sign
/// auto-refund), FAILED (synchronous provably-unpaid refund), or an operator
/// goodwill refund — never by automated post-VERIFIED reconciliation.
enum TaskX402PaymentStatus {
  PENDING
  VERIFIED
  FAILED
  REFUNDED
}

/// WHICH lever restored a payment's debit. `status` cannot answer this and the
/// admin rollup's headline quality signal depends on the answer: the operator
/// goodwill refund (VERIFIED → REFUNDED, "we charged for a bad result") and the
/// operator resolve of a wedged PENDING charge (PENDING → REFUNDED, an
/// integration or node-timeout problem) both land REFUNDED, and counting the
/// second as the first ranks a healthy agent as the worst quality-bleeding
/// endpoint — a false ranking a hostile coworker could drive on purpose by
/// wedging rows against a competitor.
///
/// Written by `attachCompensatingRefund` in the same UPDATE that mints the
/// refund transaction, so the label cannot drift from the money it describes.
/// Deliberately an explicit column rather than the implicit discriminator that
/// already exists (a goodwill refund's row always came from VERIFIED so always
/// carries `attemptId`; a resolve's never does): that invariant is a fact about
/// where finalize happens to write `attemptId` today, and a reader of the
/// rollup would have no way to know the metric silently depended on it.
enum TaskX402PaymentRefundKind {
  /// The automated refusal refund (`refundRefusedTaskX402Payment`): the node
  /// refused, the row is FAILED. Node-budget-only, user-safe, NOT a quality
  /// signal — the `failureCount` metric already counts these.
  NODE_REFUSAL
  /// The operator goodwill refund of a VERIFIED payment. The §5 quality signal.
  OPERATOR_GOODWILL
  /// The operator resolve of a wedged PENDING payment. Says nothing about the
  /// agent's output quality; counted separately so an operator still sees it.
  OPERATOR_RESOLVE
}

